  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A direct current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and an alternating current of peak value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;flow through resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> respectively. The ratio of heat produced in the two resistances in same interval of time will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0070_ba80e885d8ea.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 89px;\" /></p><p>Heat produced in resistor when direct current flows is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Heat produced in resistor when alternating current flows is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>rms</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Thus, the ratio is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}